@@ -42,9 +42,9 @@
 ## Findings worth carrying into the design discussion
 
 - **Every spend needs derivation inputs.** With unconditional re-derivation, coins of random or
-  unknown-preimage types cannot be spent; two existing ledger tests (`micro-dao`,
-  `token_vault_shielded`) spend such coins and are expected to fail for that reason; whether they do
-  is recorded by the full ledger suite run in `results.md`, not assumed here. Wallets and indexers must
+  unknown-preimage types cannot be spent; no existing ledger test spends such a coin (the
+  two tests that spend contract-owned coins, `micro-dao` and `token_vault_shielded`, use the native
+  type, which is accepted under `Empty`), so the full ledger suite passes unchanged; see `results.md`. Wallets and indexers must
   resolve `(domain separator, minting address, rule)` for every contract-minted shielded coin.
 - **Native type.** The all-zero native type is special-cased under `Empty`; any other fixed types
   (if introduced) need the same treatment or a published derivation.
diff --git a/docs/experiments/regulated-zswap-csl/results.md b/docs/experiments/regulated-zswap-csl/results.md
index 59ddd07f..2a9ce0ba 100644
--- a/docs/experiments/regulated-zswap-csl/results.md
+++ b/docs/experiments/regulated-zswap-csl/results.md
@@ -55,9 +55,43 @@ Observations recorded during the runs:
 
 Known consequences of the mandatory design, observed while building:
 
-- Every shielded spend now needs the token-type derivation inputs; coins of random
-  (underivable) types used by some existing ledger tests (`micro-dao`, `token_vault_shielded`)
-  can no longer be spent, which is the intended closure of the unguarded route and a
-  migration cost for wallets.
+- Every shielded spend now needs the token-type derivation inputs. No existing ledger test spends a
+  contract-minted shielded coin without them: the two tests that spend contract-owned coins
+  (`micro-dao`, `token_vault_shielded`) use the native all-zero type, which the relation accepts
+  under `Empty` without derivation inputs, and both pass in the full suite below. The fail-closed
+  behaviour for a coin of underivable type is shown by the zkir relation test only. The migration
+  cost for wallets (resolving the preimage of every contract-minted coin) stands.
 - The data provider still serves the legacy spend artifacts under `zswap/9/`; the ledger no
   longer uses them for spends, but their download verification keeps the legacy hash.
